        "patch_notes": "Root cause: In ContextAssetRequestHandler.handleAssetRequest, the `illegal` regex (^(web|meta)-inf.*|.*\\.tml$, case-insensitive) is matched against ChecksumPath.resourcePath BEFORE AbstractResource.forFile() resolves the path. forFile() collapses \"..\" segments (see AbstractResource lines 104-131), so an attacker-supplied extraPath such as \"checksum/../WEB-INF/web.xml\" produces resourcePath=\"../WEB-INF/web.xml\" which does NOT match the denylist (it starts with \"../\"), yet forFile() normalizes it to \"WEB-INF/web.xml\" and streams it — a directory traversal / protected-resource disclosure.\n\nFix: After calling forFile(), re-run the same `illegal` matcher against the RESOLVED resource.getPath() (which is normalized, no leading slash), and return false if it matches. Also wrap forFile() in a try/catch for IllegalStateException, which forFile() throws when the path navigates above the root (e.g. \"../../etc/...\"), returning false instead of surfacing a 500. Legitimate asset paths resolve to non-protected normalized paths and continue to stream as before. The original pre-resolution check is retained (it cheaply short-circuits direct WEB-INF/META-INF/.tml requests and preserves existing behavior for the null-root unit tests).\n\nTest: Added ensure_traversal_assets_are_rejected data-driven test covering \"../WEB-INF/...\", \"foo/../../WEB-INF/...\", \"../META-INF/...\" and \"foo/../../META-INF/...\" bypass vectors, using a mocked Context so resolution stays string-only. All 8 tests in ContextAssetRequestHandlerTest pass (verified via a temporary single-class TestNG suite; suite file restored afterward).",
