        "summary": "Fixed a CWE-022 path traversal in Tapestry's context asset handler. ContextAssetRequestHandler screened the raw request path against a WEB-INF/META-INF/*.tml denylist, but rootContextResource.forFile() subsequently normalizes \"..\" segments, so a request like \"fake-checksum/../WEB-INF/web.xml\" (or \"foo/../../WEB-INF/...\") slips past the denylist yet resolves to a protected resource. The fix re-screens the resolved resource path (after \"../\" collapsing) and rejects any attempt to navigate above the context root, blocking access to WEB-INF/META-INF while leaving legitimate asset requests unchanged."
